From: Rhnn Hur <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:47:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep only link-specific mgmt frames on their link

Since commit 46b67e5b7c49 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep a unicast management
frame on its MLO link"), mt7996_mac_write_txwi_80211() sets MT_TXD5_FL on
every unicast management frame to a station of an MLD interface. Most of
these frames are meant for the peer MLD rather than for one of its links:
mac80211 sends Block Ack frames without a link, which mt7996_tx() maps to
the primary link of the station, and hostapd answers SCS and MSCS Requests
from the BSS of the association link. A non-AP MLD that is served on its
other link while it stays in powersave on the primary link never receives
such a frame. The frame waits at the head of the AC queue of the station,
the frames queued behind it wait as well, and once MT_MAX_NON_AQL_PKT
management frames are pending, mt76 stops all TX to the station until it
reassociates.

Seen on a W1700K, an AP MLD with a 5 GHz and a 6 GHz link (Airoha AN7581
with MT7996), with two phones that are non-AP MLDs: each associated on one
link, was later served on the other one, and then lost all downlink
traffic for minutes to hours, until it reassociated. A temporary debugfs
list of the frames that the driver still held in flight showed the VO
queue of the primary link WLAN index holding MSCS Responses from hostapd
and ADDBA Responses from mac80211 and nothing else, all with MT_TXD5_FL,
up to the non-AQL limit. Data frames, which carry no MT_TXD5_FL, kept
draining from the BE queue of the same WLAN index.

Whether mac80211 named a link does not set these frames apart from the
Link Reconfiguration frames that the commit is about: mac80211 pins a
frame from the MLD address to the link that holds the channel named by
hostapd, so the MSCS Response has an explicit link, while a station sends
its Link Reconfiguration Request without one. mt76_tx_status_skb_add()
also clears info->control.flags before the TXD is written.

Set MT_TXD5_FL only on the frames that belong to their link:
- frames without MLD address translation, i.e. frames on the ALTX queue
  such as Deauthentication and Disassociation frames, which carry the
  link addresses of their TXD
- HT and VHT Action frames, e.g. SM Power Save, which mac80211 sends on
  the link it applies to
- Link Reconfiguration frames, since mac80211 removes a link before it
  sends the request and the AP MLD answers on the link of the request
- TID-To-Link Mapping frames, which hostapd answers on the link of the
  request

Other unicast management frames, e.g. Block Ack, SA Query, WNM, Radio
Measurement and Robust AV Streaming Action frames, go out again on a link
of the peer that the hardware selects.

Tested on the W1700K for about a day with the module built from this
change: one phone was served on its non-primary link for about five
hours in total, the management answers sent meanwhile left without
holding the VO queue, and no stall was seen, where one an hour was
typical before.

Fixes: 46b67e5b7c49 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: keep a unicast management frame on its MLO link")
---
 mt7996/mac.c | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/mac.c b/mt7996/mac.c
index 94c842a2..32cb00b2 100644
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -654,6 +654,55 @@ mt7996_mac_write_txwi_8023(struct mt7996_dev *dev, __le32 *txwi,
 		txwi[3] |= cpu_to_le32(MT_TXD3_HW_AMSDU);
 }
 
+/* Without MT_TXD5_FL, the hardware sends a unicast management frame to an
+ * MLD peer on a link of the peer that it selects. Most of these frames are
+ * meant for the MLD, e.g. Block Ack, SA Query, WNM and Robust AV Streaming
+ * Action frames. Fixed to a link on which the peer stays in powersave, such
+ * a frame waits in the AC queue of the station and holds the frames queued
+ * behind it. Fix the link only for frames that belong to it.
+ */
+static bool
+mt7996_mac_mgmt_fixed_link(struct sk_buff *skb, __le32 *txwi)
+{
+	struct ieee80211_mgmt *mgmt = (struct ieee80211_mgmt *)skb->data;
+
+	/* mt7996_mac_write_txwi() sets MT_TXD6_DIS_MAT on the ALTX queue: such
+	 * a frame keeps the link addresses of its TXD, e.g. deauthentication
+	 */
+	if (txwi[6] & cpu_to_le32(MT_TXD6_DIS_MAT))
+		return true;
+
+	if (!ieee80211_is_action(mgmt->frame_control) ||
+	    skb->len < IEEE80211_MIN_ACTION_SIZE(action_code))
+		return false;
+
+	/* HT and VHT Action frames are about the link they are sent on, e.g.
+	 * SM power save
+	 */
+	if (mgmt->u.action.category == WLAN_CATEGORY_HT ||
+	    mgmt->u.action.category == WLAN_CATEGORY_VHT)
+		return true;
+
+	if (mgmt->u.action.category != WLAN_CATEGORY_PROTECTED_EHT)
+		return false;
+
+	/* TID-to-link mapping and link reconfiguration frames change the links
+	 * of the MLD and stay on the link that mac80211 or hostapd chose: a
+	 * request must not leave on a link that it removes, and a response
+	 * goes on the link of its request
+	 */
+	switch (mgmt->u.action.action_code) {
+	case WLAN_PROTECTED_EHT_ACTION_TTLM_REQ:
+	case WLAN_PROTECTED_EHT_ACTION_TTLM_RES:
+	case WLAN_PROTECTED_EHT_ACTION_TTLM_TEARDOWN:
+	case WLAN_PROTECTED_EHT_ACTION_LINK_RECONFIG_REQ:
+	case WLAN_PROTECTED_EHT_ACTION_LINK_RECONFIG_RESP:
+		return true;
+	default:
+		return false;
+	}
+}
+
 static void
 mt7996_mac_write_txwi_80211(struct mt7996_dev *dev, __le32 *txwi,
 			    struct sk_buff *skb,
@@ -751,7 +800,8 @@ mt7996_mac_write_txwi_80211(struct mt7996_dev *dev, __le32 *txwi,
 
 	if (vif && ieee80211_vif_is_mld(vif) &&
 	    (multicast || unlikely(skb->protocol == cpu_to_be16(ETH_P_PAE)) ||
-	     (ieee80211_is_mgmt(fc) && wcid->sta)))
+	     (ieee80211_is_mgmt(fc) && wcid->sta &&
+	      mt7996_mac_mgmt_fixed_link(skb, txwi))))
 		txwi[5] |= cpu_to_le32(MT_TXD5_FL);
 
 	if (ieee80211_is_nullfunc(fc) && ieee80211_has_a4(fc) &&
